ed_at":"2026-06-29T20:19:16Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in v4.7.rc.custom_build [71011704c]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.rc (71011704c) - macOS Tahoe (26.5.1) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - Apple M4 Pro - Apple M4 Pro (14 threads) - 24.00 GiB memory - CoreAudio (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen a GDScript's class triggers the `MISSING_TOOL` warning, the highlight/underline appears in the LSP over the entire class (i.e., file for a non-inner-class).\n\n<img width=\"287\" height=\"105\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f54be727-eeba-4de4-89b1-801324b83f84\" />\n\nThis clutters the code display, making it difficult to recognize other warnings and errors in the file.\n\nGiven that this error is emitted when the class extends a class with the `@tool` annotation, I think it would make sense for this warning's range to encompass the `extends <CLASS_NAME>` line.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nUse the following GDScript files:\n```gdscript\n@tool\nclass_name MissingToolClass\nextends Node\n```\n\n```gdscript\nextends MissingToolClass\n\nfunc hello() -> void:\n    pass\n```\n\nNote that in the second, extending file, the whole class/file is highlighted in the LSP as having the `MISSING_TOOL` warning.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/u